## Build the Compute Image

The OpenHPC components are installed into the compute image the xCAT-native way:
the osimage's `otherpkglist` names the extra packages and `otherpkgdir` names
the repositories that provide them, and `genimage` installs them in the same
pass as the base OS -- with the copycds base repositories in context, so
dependencies resolve. `${CHROOT}` names the image directory and is used by the
customization steps later in this guide.

Before the image is built, the head node's `passwd` and `group` are copied into
it so that the service accounts `genimage` creates (munge, and the scheduler's
own) take the same UIDs and GIDs as the head. Without this, the boot-time synclist later installs
the head's credentials over image-local UIDs, leaving munge's on-disk state
orphaned so that the service fails to start.

`genimage` builds the image with `gpgcheck=0` for every repository (base and
extra alike), so the OpenHPC packages -- though signed -- are not
signature-verified at build time, consistent with how xCAT builds the base
image. Sites requiring verification should install OpenHPC on the booted nodes
instead (see the stateful recipe) or patch xCAT's `genimage`.

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Register OpenHPC components as otherpkgs on the osimage -->
```bash
# Save chroot location for the compute image
rootimgdir=$(lsdef -t osimage -o ${xcat_osimage} -i rootimgdir \
    | awk -F= '/rootimgdir=/{print $2}')
CHROOT=${rootimgdir}/rootimg
export CHROOT

# Seed the head's passwd/group so genimage's service accounts take its UIDs
mkdir -p ${CHROOT}/etc
cp /etc/passwd /etc/group ${CHROOT}/etc

# Extra repositories for the image build: OpenHPC (base + updates), EPEL, and
# CRB. The base OS repos come from the copycds tree automatically; these are the
# additions.
chdef -t osimage ${xcat_osimage} otherpkgdir="\
{{ ohpc_repo_server }}/OpenHPC/{{ ohpc_version_tree }}/{{ ostree }}/,\
{{ ohpc_repo_server }}/OpenHPC/{{ ohpc_version_tree }}/updates/{{ ostree }}/,\
{{ epel_base_url }}{{ distro_version }}/Everything/{{ arch }}/,\
{{ distro_base_url }}{{ distro_version }}/CRB/{{ arch }}/os/"

# OpenHPC packages to add on top of the base OS image
mkdir -p /install/custom/netboot/{{ distro }}
cat > /install/custom/netboot/{{ distro }}/ohpc.otherpkgs.pkglist << 'EOF'
ohpc-base-compute
{{ scheduler_compute_package }}
lmod-ohpc
chrony
EOF
chdef -t osimage ${xcat_osimage} \
    otherpkglist=/install/custom/netboot/{{ distro }}/ohpc.otherpkgs.pkglist
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Add site or pre-release OpenHPC repositories to the image build (site-specific) -->
